     #[tokio::test]
     async fn read_outline_lists_entities_one_per_line() {
         let mut d = doc(); // svc-a vertex
         let mut t = Tools::new(false);
         // 补一条边，验证 edge 行的 src→tgt 形态
         let e = r#"<mxCell id="e1" value="是" edge="1" parent="1" source="svc-a" target="svc-a"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>"#;
         let total = crate::xmlfile::total_lines(d.canonical());
         d.apply_edit(total, total, e).unwrap();
         let out = t.run(&mut d, "read", &serde_json::json!({"outline": true})).await.unwrap();
         assert!(out.text.contains("1 vertex"), "{}", out.text);
         assert!(out.text.contains("1 edge"), "{}", out.text);
         // vertex 行有 id 与标签；edge 行有 src→tgt
         assert!(out.text.contains("svc-a"), "{}", out.text);
         assert!(out.text.contains("Order Service"), "{}", out.text);
         assert!(out.text.contains("svc-a→svc-a"), "{}", out.text);
         // diagram 是容器且被标注；锚点 0/1 不出现（首个实体行是 d1）
         assert!(out.text.contains("（容器）"), "{}", out.text);
         let first_row = out.text.lines().nth(1).unwrap();
         assert!(
             first_row.trim_start().starts_with("2-"),
             "首个实体行应是 d1 容器（跳过锚点 0/1）: {first_row}"
         );
         // offset 分页：跳过第一个实体后数量减少
         let out2 = t.run(&mut d, "read", &serde_json::json!({"outline": true, "offset": 1})).await.unwrap();
         let first_rows = out.text.lines().count();
         let second_rows = out2.text.lines().count();
         assert_eq!(first_rows - second_rows, 1, "offset=1 应少显示一行");
     }

     #[tokio::test]
     async fn read_truncation_hint_names_next_range() {
         let mut xml = String::from("<mxfile><diagram id=\"d\"><mxGraphModel><root><mxCell id=\"0\"/>");
         for i in 1..=210 {
             xml.push_str(&format!(r#"<mxCell id="n{i}" value="x" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="0" width="10" height="10" as="geometry"/></mxCell>"#));
         }
         xml.push_str("</root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>");
         let mut d = XmlDoc::from_text(&xml).unwrap();
         let mut t = Tools::new(false);
         let out = t.run(&mut d, "read", &serde_json::json!({"range": "1-999"})).await.unwrap();
         assert!(out.text.contains("已截断"), "{}", &out.text[out.text.len().saturating_sub(120)..]);
         assert!(out.text.contains("续读用 range \"151-"), "应给出续读路径: {}", &out.text[out.text.len().saturating_sub(160)..]);
         assert!(out.text.lines().count() <= 160, "{}", out.text.lines().count());
     }

     #[tokio::test]
     async fn read_returns_numbered_lines() {
         let mut d = doc();
         let mut t = Tools::new(false);
         let start_line = {
             let a = d.id_to_cell("svc-a").unwrap();
             a.start_line
         };
         let end_line = {
             let a = d.id_to_cell("svc-a").unwrap();
             a.end_line
         };
         let range = format!("{start_line}-{end_line}");
         let out = t
             .run(&mut d, "read", &serde_json::json!({"range": range}))
             .await
             .unwrap();
         assert!(out.text.contains("Order Service"), "{}", out.text);
         assert!(out.text.contains(&format!("{start_line}|")));
     }
 }

parts.text:
The render is actually structurally complete: three swimlanes, external roles (用户/LLM API) with different colors (ellipse shapes, colored), all modules present, edges connecting. Quality issues:
- SSE流式 label overlaps 浏览器UI node's left edge area; edge from 用户→浏览器UI has label "SSE流式" mispositioned (it's actually the Web服务→浏览器UI SSE edge routed to 用户's position?)
- The 浏览器UI node's text is struck through by the edge from 用户 (edge crosses the node title) — the arrow enters at the middle-left overlapping the label "浏览器UI" — that's what the model was fiddling with e9/e10 anchors for!
- 服务层 swimlane header band overlaps nodes? The 服务层 title band is at top, nodes below — ok.
- Lane heights: 前端层/服务层 lanes have lots of empty bottom space; 工件层 too.
- drawio画布(iframe) — no edge from .drawio文件 to 画布? I see an edge from 无头渲染器 up to 画布 — wait spec: 文件→画布同步. The vertical edge from bottom (renderer area) up to 画布 — hmm that's e10 maybe: 文件→画布 edge routed through the right. Actually there's a long vertical edge from Agent引擎 area down... Looking: there's an edge from 画布 down to Agent引擎 (文件同步?). Eh.

Overall: ~80% good, readable, spec-faithful. The model burned turns on the 浏览器UI edge-crossing-label issue (SSE流式 label + arrow through the node title).

Now improvements to implement:

1. **Edit-loop guard** (edit same id-set consecutively ≥3 → reject with strategy advice). This directly addresses turns 25-30 burn (e9/e10 edited 3+ times consecutively).

2. **layout edge error message**: geometry_of filters edges → "cell `e10` 不存在或其几何不可读" is misleading. In layout, before geometry_of: check id_to_cell; if cell exists and is edge → Err("边没有绝对几何，不能参与 layout；调整边路由请用 edit 加拐点（<Array as=\"points\"> 放 mxGeometry 内）或锚点比例"). Need is_edge info: id_to_cell gives CellSpan with tag; edges have edge="1" attribute — not in CellSpan. Hmm. How to know it's an edge? Parse the slice: attr_value(&slice, "edge") == "1". Or geometry_of's metrics parse has is_edge. Simplest: in layout, on geometry_of None but id_to_cell Some → read slice lines and check edge attr → give specific message. Let me implement in the layout move loop:

```rust
let (x, y, w, h) = doc.geometry_of(id).ok_or_else(|| format!("cell `{id}` 不存在或其几何不可读"))?;
```
Change to:
```rust
let Some((x, y, w, h)) = doc.geometry_of(id) else {
    let reason = if doc.id_to_cell(id).is_some() {
        // 存在但几何不可读：多半是边（无绝对坐标）
        "边（edge）没有绝对几何，不能参与 layout；调整边路由请用 edit 改锚点（exitX/entryY 等）或加拐点 <Array as=\"points\">"
    } else {
        "cell 不存在"
    };
    return Err(format!("cell `{id}`: {reason}"));
};
```

3. **Anchor-fiddling loop is the same family as nudge** — the edit guard (fix 1) covers it.

Also consider: should view+edit closed loop be dampened more fundamentally? The edit guard with consecutive same-ids threshold 3 is targeted. Let me implement:

In Tools::edit — after successful apply, compute changed ids... but the guard should PREVENT (reject before applying? or after?). Simpler: key by the RANGE spec(s) touched? No — model may edit same cell via different ranges (batch ranges covering it). Key by ids known BEFORE apply: for range-based edits we don't know affected ids until diff. But we know the requested ranges (line numbers). Alternative: track after-apply changed ids, and reject NEXT time? A post-hoc counter doesn't prevent the 3rd edit...

Design: in edit() after successful apply, get report.changed; update counter: if changed set == last_changed set → streak += 1 else streak = 1, last_changed = set. If streak >= 2 (i.e. this is the 3rd consecutive edit of the same id set) → we've ALREADY applied it. Rejecting post-apply is wrong (work done). 

Alternative: BEFORE applying, resolve ranges → affected cells pre-span (like off_range uses pre-spans). The requested ranges can be matched against pre-edit cell spans: cells whose spans intersect the ranges = will-be-touched. Compute id set, check counter, reject before apply. Feasible: ranges resolved as (start,end) line pairs; cells() spans intersect. For batch edits same. For draw (whole) skip.

Implement in edit():
- build ranges: Vec<(usize,usize)> from resolved args (whole → skip guard).
- touched: doc.cells() pre-edit spans intersecting any range → ids (exclude container cells? fine to include).
- sorted ids key; counter: same as nudge: consecutive same-set count since... reset when? On view? No. The loop is edit,view,edit — views shouldn't reset. Reset on: successful edit of a DIFFERENT id set (streak reset to 1), or draw. Since it's "consecutive same-set edits" semantics, the streak lives across views/reads — correct for catching the fiddling loop.
- threshold: reject at count >= 2 prior (3rd occurrence). Message: "同一组 cell（…）已连续 edit 2 次仍未收敛——别再对同一处做第 3 次微调：要么接受现状收尾（reply done），要么换策略（draw 重画该区域 / 调整锚点为 0..1 比例值组合 / 接受残余视觉瑕疵）。"

Wait — threshold: turns 26 & 29 edited [e9,e10] (changed=2 both). With guard, 3rd would be rejected. In the trace, [e9,e10] was edited exactly twice (turns 26, 29) after separate e9 (turn ~12) and e10 (turn ~10) singles. Consecutive same-set: turns 26,29 → streak 2. The 30-turn burn also included earlier singles. With threshold 2-prior-reject-at-3rd, this run would have been cut at the 3rd [e9,e10] edit — saving ~1 turn only?? Hmm wait — after rejection at 3rd, no_progress streak also kicks in if model keeps fiddling (rejected → +1 each). Model tries 4th → reject (+2)... reaches 6 → abort. Actually better: rejection message tells model to wrap up; if it instead re-fiddles with slightly different ids... eh.

Actually — hmm, is 3rd-rejection the right threshold? Let me reconsider: legit same-set consecutive edits: (1) edit value, then (2) edit style of same cell — plausible in one task. 3rd consecutive edit of same set is rarely legit. Keep reject at 3rd.

But also the no-progress streak: edits here DO change content (progress), so they don't feed it. The edit guard is the right tool.

Also update the nudge reset semantics: nudge_counts reset on edit success — but now edit itself is guarded separately; fine.

Wait, subtle: reset of the edit-streak. Where does it live? Tools::edit is called for both edit and draw (whole=true). Track: last_edit_ids: Option<String> + edit_streak: u32. In edit() non-whole success: compute changed set AFTER apply... for the NEXT call's comparison I need the ids of what was JUST edited. Post-apply diff ids are known (report.changed). Use that (post-hoc record): streak = if changed == last_changed { streak+1 } else { 1 }. But prevention needs pre-check BEFORE apply for the CURRENT call: compare current requested-touched ids against last_changed. So:
- pre-compute touched ids from ranges ∩ pre-spans
- if touched == last_changed && edit_streak >= 2 → reject
- apply; on success set last_changed = touched (or report.changed? use touched for consistency), edit_streak = if touched == last_changed {streak+1} else {1}

Simpler: 
```rust
let key = touched_ids.join(",");
if self.last_edit_key.as_deref() == Some(key.as_str()) { self.edit_streak += 1; } else { self.edit_streak = 1; self.last_edit_key = Some(key); }
if self.edit_streak > 2 { return Err(...) }  // 3rd consecutive same-set
```
Hmm but if rejected, streak keeps growing — subsequent different-set edit resets to 1 ✓.

Edge: ranges that touch MANY cells (big range) — key huge; fine.

Also: should check/no-op count? no-op edits (report.noop) — the model retried identical edit → no-op → consecutive guard catches. OK.

Draw (whole=true) resets: self.edit_streak = 0, last_edit_key=None — new content. ✓

4. Also fix layout error for edges.

Test additions:
- edit guard test: 3 consecutive edits to cell a (different text each time) → 3rd rejected; then edit to b succeeds (reset); 
- layout edge error test: doc with edge, layout move on edge id → err contains "边".

Let me implement. In Tools struct: replace nudge tracking? Add fields: last_edit_key: Option<String>, edit_streak: u32.

Where in edit(): need ranges resolved BEFORE apply. In batch branch, ranges resolved via resolve_arg into `batch` vec of (start,end,text). In whole branch skip. Compute touched ids after building batch:

```rust
// 同组连续 edit 守卫：同一批 cell 连续第 3 次被 edit → 拒绝（E2E 实测
// 锚点视觉微调循环）。范围触达的 cell 用前置 span 求交。
let touched: Vec<String> = {
    let mut ids: Vec<String> = doc.cells().iter()
        .filter(|c| batch.iter().any(|&(s, e, _)| !(c.end_line < s || c.start_line > e)))
        .map(|c| c.id.clone())
        .collect();
    ids.sort(); ids.dedup();
    ids
};
let key = touched.join(",");
if self.last_edit_key.as_deref() == Some(key.as_str()) {
    self.edit_streak += 1;
} else {
    self.edit_streak = 1;
    self.last_edit_key = Some(key.clone());
}
if self.edit_streak > 2 { ... Err ... }
```

Careful: mutating self before apply — if apply FAILS afterwards, the counter advanced... acceptable (failed edit → model may retry same → would be rejected as 3rd... hmm that's harsh: a failed edit + successful same edit = streak 2 → allowed. failed,failed,success → 3rd rejected but that success... wait streak increments on each CALL including failed applies. Failed edit doesn't change file but counts. Retrying a failed edit with same ranges → streak 2 → ok; another → rejected. Hmm — failed→fix sequence is legit (parse error recovery as seen in trace! turn 24 failed ill-formed, turn 25 succeeded SAME ranges). With my guard: turn 24 call: streak=1 (rejected by parse). turn 25 call same ranges: streak=2 → allowed ✓. A third identical-ranges call would be rejected — but that would be a genuine fix-loop. OK good.

But placement: guard check must happen for BOTH single and batch path — the batch vec exists in both (single → vec![(...)]). Put the guard right before apply_edits. Note `doc.cells()` — pre-edit ✓. Borrow: doc.cells() borrowed while building batch... batch is Vec<String> owned, fine.

One more: reject message must include the no-progress note? The rejection is an Err from tool → wrapped "工具执行失败: ..." → feeds no_progress streak ✓.

Also on draw (whole): reset edit_streak/last_edit_key.

Implement now. Also layout edge message.

