User says: relax the edit guard a bit. Current: reject at 3rd consecutive edit of same cell set (edit_streak > 2, i.e. calls 1,2 allowed, 3rd rejected). Relax options:

1. Raise threshold to 4th call (allow 3 consecutive edits of the same set).
2. Don't reset state on rejection (currently I reset edit_streak=0 and last_edit_key=None on rejection — that means after a rejection the model can start a NEW streak immediately! That's actually a bug making it MORE lenient than intended: reject → model edits same set again → streak starts at 1 again... wait no: on rejection I reset to 0/None, so next same-set edit → streak=1, allowed, then 2, then 3rd rejected again. That makes the guard nearly useless — it rejects every 3rd call in an infinite fiddle loop. Need to keep the state on rejection so subsequent same-set edits keep being rejected. Let me fix that while relaxing threshold.)

3. Also failed edits (parse errors) currently count toward streak — relax: only count successful applies? The trace showed parse-fail → retry same ranges (legit recovery). If failed edits count: fail(1), success(2), next same-set(3rd) rejected — harsh. Better: only count on SUCCESSFUL apply. But the pre-apply check happens before knowing success... restructure: check streak only against SUCCESSFUL history: increment streak post-apply (on success), and PRE-check before apply: if this call's touched set == last successful set && streak >= N → reject. On failed apply, don't touch counters.

Let me restructure:
- Fields: last_edit_key, edit_streak (successful same-set consecutive count).
- Pre-check: if touched==last_key && edit_streak >= 2 → reject (3rd successful consecutive... wait: streak counts successful same-set edits; pre-check at call time: if last_key==touched && streak >= 2 → this would be the 3rd consecutive → reject. Allows 2 consecutive same-set edits (relaxed from... originally allowed 2, rejected 3rd — same!). Hmm original: edit_streak incremented per call including failures; >2 → reject at 3rd call.

User wants more relaxed. Options: allow 3 consecutive same-set successful edits, reject at 4th (threshold streak >= 3). And only successful edits count (parse-fail retries free). And keep state on rejection (don't reset) so the fiddle loop stays blocked; the no-progress streak in turn_loop will abort the loop after 6 stalls anyway.

So new logic:

```rust
