The nesting is off: after my edit, `match self.ensure_renderer().await { Ok(renderer) => match reroute { ... }, Err(e) => {...} }` — the closing braces need fixing. Current structure:

```rust
if self.render {
    match self.ensure_renderer().await {
        Ok(renderer) => match renderer.reroute(doc.canonical()).await {
            Ok(new_xml) => { ... return ...; }
            Err(e) => {
                eprintln!(...);
            }
        }
    }   // <-- missing close for ensure_renderer match?
}
```

Let me look at the tail — after `eprintln` there's `}` `}` `}` then comment. Count: Ok(new_xml) match arm ends `};` then `Err(e) => { eprintln; }` closes reroute match... then need `}` for ensure_renderer match arm? Actually `Ok(renderer) => match reroute...` — the match on ensure_renderer needs its Err arm too! Current code: `Err(e) => { eprintln }` was intended for the REROUTE error (fallback), but ensure_renderer's Err should also fall through (deterministic). Restructure cleanly:

```rust
if self.render {
    if let Ok(renderer) = self.ensure_renderer().await {
        match renderer.reroute(doc.canonical()).await {
            Ok(new_xml) => { ... return ...; }
            Err(e) => eprintln!("libavoid reroute 不可用，回退确定性路由: {e}"),
        }
    }
}
```

Rewrite that block.

