parts.text:
Plan:

**Backend** (minimal): add `#[serde(default)] pub cell_ids: Vec<String>` to HistoryRec; set `cell_ids: req.cell_ids.clone()` in rec1 (self-check rec2 gets empty). Serde default keeps old histories loading.

**Frontend**:
1. **Enter to send**: keydown on #input — Enter without shift and not composing (e.isComposing) → preventDefault + submit form (`$('chatform').requestSubmit()` or call onsubmit logic). Careful: busy → submit acts as cancel! If busy, Enter sending would trigger cancelJob — bad. Guard: only submit when !busy. Shift+Enter = newline (default). IME composition (Chinese input) — e.isComposing or keyCode===229 → don't send.

2. **Quote badge**: 
   - New `logUser(text, ids)` function that creates div.msg.user, appends a badge element (e.g. `<span class="ref-badge">📎 引用 N</span>`) then textContent. Badge above/before text.
   - Use in onsubmit when ids.length>0; and in renderHistoryIntoChat with r.cell_ids.
   - Design: small pill badge at top of the bubble. Style: `.ref-badge { display:inline-block; font-size:11px; padding:2px 8px; margin-bottom:4px; border-radius:999px; background:rgba(255,255,255,.12); color:#9db4e8; border:1px solid rgba(157,180,232,.35); }` and show ids in title attr. Maybe with 📎. Full bubble style stays.

Also make badge clickable? Could re-select cells — canvas selection — nice but requires selecting in current canvas; keep simple, but title shows ids. Actually let me make the badge show ids text: "📎 svc-a, db" if ≤3 ids else "📎 引用 5 个 cell". Clicking re-selects those cells on canvas (if same session & mxGraph mode) — that's a nice touch but drawio iframe mode selection goes through plugin... skip click behavior for now, keep QoL simple. Hmm — user said "我不确定我喜欢什么样式设计，你先自己试试" — so provide a tasteful design they can tweak.

Also: sel-note "（附带 N 个 cell 引用）" already shows before sending. The badge duplicates post-send. Fine.

Implement:

web.rs / history.rs:
- HistoryRec add field:
```rust
/// 引用选中 cell 的 ids（UI 徽章用；旧历史无此字段 → 空）
#[serde(default)]
pub cell_ids: Vec<String>,
```
- mk_rec signature add ids param; rec1 uses req.cell_ids.clone(), rec2 empty.

Wait mk_rec is a closure; add param `ids: Vec<String>`.

app.js:
- keydown handler:
```js
$('input').addEventListener('keydown', (ev) => {
  if (ev.key !== 'Enter' || ev.shiftKey) return;
  if (ev.isComposing || ev.keyCode === 229) return; // 输入法组词
  if (busy) return; // 任务运行中 Enter = 取消的歧义太危险，不触发
  ev.preventDefault();
  $('chatform').requestSubmit();
});
```
requestSubmit triggers onsubmit ✓ (modern browsers).

- logUser:
```js
function logUser(text, ids) {
  const div = document.createElement('div');
  div.className = 'msg user';
  if (ids && ids.length) {
    const b = document.createElement('span');
    b.className = 'ref-badge';
    const list = ids.join(', ');
    b.textContent = ids.length <= 3 ? `📎 ${list}` : `📎 引用 ${ids.length} 个 cell`;
    b.title = '选中引用随消息发送：' + list;
    div.appendChild(b);
  }
  div.appendChild(document.createTextNode(text));
  $('chatlog').appendChild(div);
  $('chatlog').scrollTop = $('chatlog').scrollHeight;
}
```
- onsubmit: `log('user', text)` → `logUser(text, ids)`.
- renderHistoryIntoChat: `logMsg('user', r.user)` → need badge: replace with a logUserMsg variant appending to chatlog without scroll (final scroll at end). Reuse logUser but it scrolls — fine, it's called per record; final scroll at end ok. But logUser appends & scrolls; renderHistoryIntoChat has its own final scroll — acceptable.

Wait renderHistoryIntoChat uses logMsg which doesn't scroll; logUser scrolls each time — minor perf, fine.

style.css: add .ref-badge styles + white-space handling. .msg.user has white-space: pre-wrap from .msg — badge span inside pre-wrap... text node will respect pre-wrap ✓.

CSS:
```css
.ref-badge { display: inline-block; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.4; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 0 0 6px; border-radius: 999px; background: rgba(157,180,232,.14); color: #9db4e8; border: 1px solid rgba(157,180,232,.35); cursor: default; }
.msg.user { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }  // hmm — user bubble is block with pre-wrap text; adding flex column so badge sits on its own line. But text node inside flex container becomes anonymous flex item — pre-wrap preserved within it. OK.
```
Actually careful: making .msg.user flex might break multi-line text wrapping (anonymous flex item wraps fine). Simpler: badge as block with display:block; width:fit-content — no flex needed:
```css
.ref-badge { display: block; width: fit-content; ... margin-bottom: 6px; }
```
That's clean.

Also cursor default; add title tooltip already.

Now — do streams: when user sends, ids captured; badge shows. Replay reads r.cell_ids. SELFCHECK rec2 has empty cell_ids ✓ no badge.

Tests: cargo test workspace — history tests may construct HistoryRec literally; adding a field breaks struct literals (need cell_ids added in tests). Let me grep HistoryRec literal usages.

